# "Other world" palette: the same keys as night-school.pal with new colours.
# Swapping palettes turns any scene into its other-world version without
# separate tiles (see docs/design-references.md 2.3, "world change = palette
# change"). Rust, dried blood and bone instead of night blues; spirits turn
# acid green. Keep this file's keys identical to night-school.pal.
K 0a0507 outline, deepest shadow
D 24090f dried-blood dark
N 3a1018 crimson shadow
U 4e1c22 rust red
u 6e2a2c rust red light
M a0503a ember glow (replaces moonlight)
W a89a7c ash plaster
w d8ccb0 bone highlight
G 3a2a18 rotten wood dark
g 5a4024 rotten wood
p 3a1a14 charred wood dark
P 5a2a1c charred wood
s c8a888 pale skin
h 8a6458 pale skin shadow
H 1a1012 hair
R ff4a2a accent red (brighter)
r 8a1a14 accent red dark
Y d8b048 dim gold
C b8f070 spirit acid green
c 5a9a3a spirit green dark
S 32181b occult shade (blend of D and w)
V 651b1d bruise violet (blend of U and r)
m a2352b rose (blend of u and R)
n 603624 plaster deep shadow (blend of N and Y)
b 776b58 plaster shadow (blend of W and H)
o 7a4c27 wood light (blend of P and Y)
q 8a2c25 skin deep shadow (blend of U and R)
O ed7838 candle flame (blend of R and Y)
L d8c9a3 flame core (blend of w and Y)
